  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tracking progress and official development assistance needs towards Achieving SDG2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the ongoing uptake, implementation and monitoring of the Ceres2030 recommendations and its approaches with various partners while improving the efficiency and effectiveness of official development assistance (ODA) for agriculture and food security. Ceres2030 is a Report on Sustainable Solutions to End Hunger represented a first ever evidence-based global road map, published in the scientific journal Nature, of the 10 high impact areas and the additional public investment needed, to end hunger, double the incomes and productivity of small-scale producers, and protect the climate as agreed in SDG 2.</narrative>
  </description>
